  "abstract": "MeanFlow Transformers with Representation Autoencoders trains MeanFlow in a Representation Autoencoder latent space to enable efficient guidance-free one-step and few-step image generation. The method combines RAE latents and a DiT-DH backbone with Consistency Mid-Training initialization, MeanFlow Distillation, optional MeanFlow Training bootstrapping, and finite-difference transport derivatives. It reaches 1-step FID 2.03 on ImageNet 256 while reducing sampling GFLOPS and total training cost compared with vanilla MeanFlow.",
